NUM-24: count the right end wall of a transect like the left one

getFlow() closed the last sub-section at the last real station
(k == Nstations - 1). The vertical wall that transect_validate() adds at the
right end is the slice after it; it has no area, so its own flow is zero and
its wetted perimeter was dropped, while the left end wall is carried into the
first sub-section. Close a transect's last sub-section at the wall slice
instead (LastSlice = Nstations), so both end walls count, as the reference
manual's algorithm prescribes. Streets keep Nstations - 1, so their results do
not change.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply NUM-24_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/transect.c b/src/legacy/engine/transect.c
index c8e58ca..518dbe9 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/transect.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/transect.c
@@ -44,6 +44,7 @@ static double  Xrightbank;             // station where right overbank begins
 static double  Xfactor;                // multiplier for station spacing
 static double  Yfactor;                // factor added to station elevations
 static double  Lfactor;                // main channel/flood plain length
+static int     LastSlice;              // slice that ends the last sub-section
 
 //-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 //  External functions (declared in funcs.h)   
@@ -253,6 +254,10 @@ void  transect_validate(int j)
     Station[Nstations] = Station[Nstations-1];
     Elev[Nstations] = Elev[0];
 
+    // --- the right end wall belongs to the last sub-section, as the
+    //     left end wall belongs to the first one
+    LastSlice = Nstations;
+
     // --- create geometry tables
     Transect[j].nTbl = N_TRANSECT_TBL;
     createTables(&Transect[j], ymin, ymax);
@@ -560,7 +565,7 @@ double getFlow(int k, double a, double wp, int findFlow)
     if ( findFlow == FALSE)
     {
         // --- flow needs updating if we are at last station
-        if ( k == Nstations - 1 ) findFlow = TRUE;
+        if ( k == LastSlice ) findFlow = TRUE;
 
         // --- flow needs updating if we are at end of left overbank and
         //     there is a change in Manning's n and section not vertical
@@ -683,6 +688,9 @@ void  transect_createStreetTransect(TStreet* street)
         street->transect.nTbl = N_TRANSECT_TBL;
     }
 
+    // --- the last slice (crown or right sidewalk) forms its own sub-section
+    LastSlice = Nstations - 1;
+
     // --- assign Manning's N to street
     Nchannel = street->roughness;
     if (street->backWidth == 0.0)
